title: SciForge-OSS
version: 1.6.0
message: >-
  If you use SciForge-OSS in your research, please cite it
  as described below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: SciForge
    family-names: OSS Team
    affiliation: SciForge Project
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: https://gitcode.com/GewisLab/SciForge-OSS
repository-code: https://gitcode.com/GewisLab/SciForge-OSS.git
abstract: >-
  A pure Skill-driven AI Scientist framework whose method is
  domain-agnostic and whose capability envelope is code-runnable
  science: any field whose methodology can be executed as code,
  data, and literature work on a machine or GPU cluster (numerical/
  symbolic simulation, ML/statistics, causal inference, and
  web-search-augmented humanities). Domains requiring proprietary
  or GUI-bound solvers (commercial CFD, COMSOL) or wet-lab hardware
  are out of scope unless reducible to a scriptable pipeline.
  Demonstrated across physics, mathematics, computer science,
  medicine, economics, education, materials science, earth science,
  and more.
keywords:
  - AI for Science
  - AI Scientist
  - Scientific Research Automation
  - DAG-based Research
  - Skill-driven Framework
